-- title:
--   Section 3 — Cubicity, connectedness, and minimum face arity
-- statement:
--   Every dart-minimal counterexample in the admissible class is
--   cubic, connected, and has no face with fewer than five darts:
--   $$\operatorname{MinimalCounterexample}(H)\Longrightarrow
--   \operatorname{Cubic}(H)\land\operatorname{Connected}(H)\land
--   \forall d\in D,\quad 5\le a(d),$$
--   where $a(d)$ is the cardinality of the face orbit containing $d$.
--
--   Formalization note: a conjunction of three source results. Cubicity follows
--   from the precubic comparison class, connectedness from component reduction,
--   and the face-arity bound from the local/Birkhoff reductions. This statement
--   does not claim the stronger small-ring Birkhoff theorem or configuration
--   embedding theory; those remain part of the finite-case-analysis development.
--
--   Notation: $D=\{0,\ldots,n-1\}$ is the dart set, $n = |D|$ its
--   size, and $p = \nu_H$ is the node permutation. Write $e,f$ for the edge and face
--   permutations, with $p(f(e(d)))=d$. Edge, node and face counts $E,N,F$ are numbers
--   of permutation orbits, including singleton orbits. The component count $C$ uses
--   the equivalence generated by all three permutations. Planarity means the exact
--   Euler equality $E+N+F=n+2C$, and connectedness means $C=1$.
--
--   A plain hypermap has a fixed-point-free involution $e$. Cubic means every node
--   orbit has size three; precubic means every node orbit has size at most three.
--   Bridgeless means $d$ and $e(d)$ never lie in the same face orbit. A $k$-coloring
--   is a map $D\to\{0,\ldots,k-1\}$ constant on face orbits and different across
--   each edge step. No requirement uses all available colors. The empty dart set
--   has zero components, is planar, and is colorable, but is not connected.
--
--   An admissible hypermap is planar, bridgeless, plain and precubic. A minimal
--   counterexample is a non-four-colorable admissible hypermap such that every
--   admissible hypermap with fewer darts is four-colorable. Minimality includes
--   all finite carriers through their enumeration by $\operatorname{Fin}(m)$;
--   cubicity, connectedness and lower face-degree bounds are not assumed.
--
--   Source: Georges Gonthier, A Computer-Checked Proof of the Four Colour Theorem (2005), https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/wp-content/uploads/2012/10/4colproof.pdf; Section 3, PDF p. 7, paragraph on PDF p. 7 discussing local reductions, and PDF p. 8, Birkhoff discussion; Section 5.4, PDF pp. 38–39. Relevant displays are unnumbered. Pinned executable reference: https://github.com/rocq-community/fourcolor/blob/c1d6b1cd5288bea4b067aac13cdde3c18dffe018/theories/proof/coloring.v#L233; https://github.com/rocq-community/fourcolor/blob/c1d6b1cd5288bea4b067aac13cdde3c18dffe018/theories/proof/patch.v#L619; https://github.com/rocq-community/fourcolor/blob/c1d6b1cd5288bea4b067aac13cdde3c18dffe018/theories/proof/birkhoff.v#L493.
-- source:
--   Georges Gonthier, A Computer-Checked Proof of the Four Colour Theorem (2005), https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/wp-content/uploads/2012/10/4colproof.pdf; Section 3, PDF p. 7, paragraph on PDF p. 7 discussing local reductions, and PDF p. 8, Birkhoff discussion; Section 5.4, PDF pp. 38–39. Relevant displays are unnumbered. Pinned executable reference: https://github.com/rocq-community/fourcolor/blob/c1d6b1cd5288bea4b067aac13cdde3c18dffe018/theories/proof/coloring.v#L233; https://github.com/rocq-community/fourcolor/blob/c1d6b1cd5288bea4b067aac13cdde3c18dffe018/theories/proof/patch.v#L619; https://github.com/rocq-community/fourcolor/blob/c1d6b1cd5288bea4b067aac13cdde3c18dffe018/theories/proof/birkhoff.v#L493.

import Definitions.Def_FourColor_Hypermap

namespace FourColor
universe u
theorem minimal_counterexample_structure :
  ∀ (n : ℕ) (H : Hypermap n), H.MinimalCounterexample →
    H.Cubic ∧ H.Connected ∧ ∀ x : Fin n, 5 ≤ H.faceArity x := by sorry
end FourColor
